IMPORT prelude

-- Codex Insurance Limited — policy coverage determination.
--
-- Encodes fixtures/chubb-policy.txt as a function from a claim's facts
-- (`Claim`) to whether a benefit is payable on that claim (`covered`).
-- Comment references (e.g. "1.1", "2.1", "3.2.1") are the source
-- contract's own section numbers.

§ `Fact schema`
-- DECLAREs and helpers below this marker are copied verbatim from
-- bench/schema-l4.md, per the task's output contract. Do not edit them
-- independently of that source.

DECLARE Ground IS ONE OF Sickness, `Accidental injury`, Neither

DECLARE Cause IS ONE OF
  Skydiving, `Military service`, Firefighting, `Police service`, Other

DECLARE Claim
  HAS `agreement signed`                           IS A BOOLEAN
      `premium paid month`                         IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `hospitalization month`                      IS A NUMBER
      `hospitalization ground`                     IS A Ground
      `age at hospitalization`                     IS A NUMBER
      `causes`                                     IS A LIST OF Cause
      `fraud month`                                IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `misrepresentation month`                    IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `wellness visit month`                       IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `wellness visit provider qualified`          IS A BOOLEAN
      `written confirmation month`                 IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `dispute arisen`                             IS A BOOLEAN
      `unable to settle month`                     IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `arbitration commenced month`                IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `valid arbitration award issued`             IS A BOOLEAN
      `written proof of claim month`               IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `recovery sought month`                      IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `policy term months`                         IS A NUMBER

GIVEN  `event month` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
       `limit month` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`no later than` MEANS
  CONSIDER `event month`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST m  THEN m AT MOST `limit month`

GIVEN  cs IS A LIST OF Cause
       c  IS A Cause
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`arose out of` MEANS elem c cs

§ `1 — Policy in effect and conditions`

-- 1.3 No later than the 7th month anniversary of the effective date,
-- written confirmation of a wellness visit (occurring no later than the
-- 6th month anniversary) with a qualified medical provider must be
-- supplied.
--
-- Read together with the 1.1-condition-3 language ("is still pending or
-- has been satisfied in a timely fashion"): a fact not yet on record is
-- not yet a breach as long as its own deadline has not yet arrived, as of
-- the hospitalization. Once a month value is actually on record, only its
-- value against the fixed deadline matters — see NOTES.md for why "still
-- pending" is read as applying only to the not-yet-recorded case.

GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`confirmation limb met` claim MEANS
        `no later than` (claim's `written confirmation month`) 7
    OR  (    isNothing (claim's `written confirmation month`)
         AND claim's `hospitalization month` LESS THAN 7)

GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`wellness visit limb met` claim MEANS
        (    `no later than` (claim's `wellness visit month`) 6
         AND claim's `wellness visit provider qualified`)
    OR  (    isNothing (claim's `wellness visit month`)
         AND claim's `hospitalization month` LESS THAN 6)

GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`condition 1.3 met` claim MEANS
        `confirmation limb met` claim
    AND `wellness visit limb met` claim

-- 1.2 Cancelation is deemed to have occurred on fraud, on misrepresentation
-- (read here as covering "material withholding of information" too, since
-- the fact schema carries no field of its own for withholding — see
-- NOTES.md), on a section-1.3 failure, or on automatic expiry at the end
-- of the policy term.

GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`policy canceled` claim MEANS
        isJust (claim's `fraud month`)
    OR  isJust (claim's `misrepresentation month`)
    OR  NOT (`condition 1.3 met` claim)
    OR  claim's `hospitalization month` GREATER THAN claim's `policy term months`

-- 1.1 The policy is in effect at the time of the hospitalization only if
-- all four numbered conditions hold.

GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`premium paid on time` claim MEANS
    `no later than` (claim's `premium paid month`) (claim's `hospitalization month`)

GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`policy in effect at hospitalization` claim MEANS
        claim's `agreement signed`
    AND `premium paid on time` claim
    AND `condition 1.3 met` claim
    AND NOT (`policy canceled` claim)

-- 1.1 chapeau: a benefit is payable only for a hospitalization for
-- sickness or accidental injury — not for a hospitalization due to a
-- deliberate, non-accidental act (`Neither`).

GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`ground is sickness or accidental injury` claim MEANS
    CONSIDER claim's `hospitalization ground`
    WHEN Sickness             THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Accidental injury`  THEN TRUE
    WHEN Neither              THEN FALSE

§ `2 — General exclusions`

-- 2.1 No benefit is paid for an event arising directly or indirectly out
-- of skydiving, military service, firefighting, or police service, or
-- where the claimant's age at hospitalization is 80 or above.

GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`excluded event` claim MEANS
        `arose out of` (claim's `causes`) Skydiving
    OR  `arose out of` (claim's `causes`) `Military service`
    OR  `arose out of` (claim's `causes`) Firefighting
    OR  `arose out of` (claim's `causes`) `Police service`
    OR  claim's `age at hospitalization` AT LEAST 80

§ `3 — General conditions`

-- 3.2.1 Arbitration is a condition precedent to Our liability whenever a
-- dispute or disagreement has arisen: arbitration must be commenced
-- within three months of the parties becoming unable to settle, and the
-- issuance of a valid arbitration award is itself a further condition
-- precedent. Failing to commence arbitration on time extinguishes the
-- claim entirely, which this models as the same "not satisfied" outcome.

GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`arbitration commenced on time` claim MEANS
    CONSIDER claim's `unable to settle month`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
    WHEN JUST u  THEN `no later than` (claim's `arbitration commenced month`) (u PLUS 3)

GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`arbitration condition satisfied` claim MEANS
        NOT claim's `dispute arisen`
    OR  (    `arbitration commenced on time` claim
         AND claim's `valid arbitration award issued`)

-- 3.2.1 "In no case shall You seek to recover on this Policy before the
-- expiration of sixty (60) days after written proof of claim has been
-- submitted." The fact schema is month-grained, so 60 days is
-- approximated as 2 months here — a unit-conversion judgement call
-- recorded in NOTES.md.

GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`recovery timing condition satisfied` claim MEANS
    CONSIDER claim's `recovery sought month`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
    WHEN JUST r  THEN CONSIDER claim's `written proof of claim month`
                        WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
                        WHEN JUST p  THEN r AT LEAST (p PLUS 2)

§ `Coverage determination`

GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE covered claim IF
        `ground is sickness or accidental injury` claim
    AND `policy in effect at hospitalization` claim
    AND NOT (`excluded event` claim)
    AND `arbitration condition satisfied` claim
    AND `recovery timing condition satisfied` claim
